## 4. First-Principles Fixes Applied (2026-09-01)

### 4.1 Version drift
lsp.oo:17 and lsp_extras.oo:106 both returned 2.9.2. ooda.pkg pins 2.10.0; every other governance board says 2.10.0. Both updated to call lsp_version(), which now returns 2.10.0.

### 4.2 Strict prefix in lsp_server_uri_is_under
The original 8-line implementation accepted any root as a prefix of uri. A URI like file:///wsxx would be considered under root file:///ws. The fixed 6-line implementation requires uri == root OR the next character after the root prefix is /. This closes a path-boundary bypass in workspace trust.

### 4.3 Init-before-use error envelope (DEFERRED)
Current lsp_server.oo:124 returns empty string for pre-initialize text-bearing requests. The proper fix is a -32602 JSON-RPC error envelope. Deferred to keep lsp_server.oo under 256.

## 5. Double-Run Test Proof

The wrapper at ooda/lsp_double_run_v2.oo imports lsp/mod.oo, lsp/lsp_jsonrpc.oo, lsp/lsp_protocol.oo, lsp/lsp_server.oo, lsp/lsp_symbol_index.oo, lsp/lsp_hover.oo, lsp/lsp_definition.oo, lsp/lsp_stdlib_scan.oo, lsp/lsp_discovery.oo and runs six probes:
1. lsp_version returns deterministic 2.10.0.
2. lsp_protocol_frame round-trips byte-identical.
3. lsp_index_prefix deterministic on a known prefix.
4. lsp_def_resolve deterministic for FsReadCap.
5. lsp_hover_from_index deterministic for a known symbol.
6. lsp_server_extract_diags deterministic for a sample document.

The test is executed twice in env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin with a clean shell, capturing the byte-identical stdout and exit codes.

