## 7. Open Gaps (carried over from 2026-08-31 plus new)

1. No real compiler integration. Hover, definition, codeAction, formatting only see canonical stdlib symbols. RFC 0006 §6 has a draft LSP-facing API. UNCHANGED.
2. No textDocument/documentLink on hover, no textDocument/inlayHint on completion, no workspace/executeCommand on the stdlib index. UNCHANGED.
3. No live double-run certification of the 5 smoke tests from the 2026-08-31 audit. The ooda/scripts/lsp_*.oo and ooda/scripts/std_qa/std_qa_lsp_*.oo use the import pattern lsp/... which resolves to ooda/scripts/lsp/... and fails at compile time. The compiler rejects ../ for security. The 5 proofs cannot be run as written. NEW GAP. The wrapper ooda/lsp_double_run_v2.oo provides a runnable subset of the probes.
4. Init-before-use text-bearing requests return empty string instead of a -32602 JSON-RPC error envelope. DEFERRED for cap margin.
5. The 2026-08-31 audit dossier at openOODA/audit/lsp_redteam_2026_08_31.oot is historical. §2 capabilities and §10 line counts are now stale. This audit (2026-09-01) supersedes those sections.

